Z||000000||Zorba||10-31-2000||01:48 PM||||This is my interpretation of the V8 wiring set up for a carburated engine. Can you tell me if these wires are routed correctly. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/v8wiring.JPG"> <BR>What am i missing here?<P>Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-31-2000||05:05 PM||||Zorba,<P>I think your making this harder than it really is. For a carborated motor, the wiring is very simple:<P>HEI: needs constant 12 volt when ignition key is "on" and in crank position.<P>Tach: Directly attaches to the HEI. You will need to recalibrate the stock tach but, the tach is not needed to make the motor run.<P>Starter: Use the existing starter wires. You may need to make them longer but they should be wired the same.<P>Alternator: Use stock wiring.<P>The only other thing you may need to wire is an electric choke. There you just follow the manufacturer's directions.<P>Someone please correct me if I'm wrong.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000002||Archie||10-31-2000||10:02 PM||||Mario...... what year is your Fiero? Is it an Automatic or a stick? Do you still have the original ECM and wire harness in it? & I'll just tell you by wire colors. If I do that, you gotta actually do it the way I tell you and not a combination of the way you think it should be done and the way I'll tell you how to do it by wire colors. If your one of the guys who took out the original ECM and harness then your on your own.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zorba||11-01-2000||03:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Mario...... what year is your Fiero? Is it an Automatic or a stick? Do you still have the original ECM and wire harness in it?  (edited 10-31-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The car is an 86 SE, manual, 5 speed ISUZU, with the ECM and wiring harness all in it. It's a electric choke, carburated 307 with ram horns for headers.<P>I will faithfully follow your instructions.<BR>Here's a list of challenges:<P>1.I am not sure if I have to use the junction box or not.<BR>Explanation: it seems that the water gauge sensor wires (dark green) don't come from the wiring harness on the firewall. All I see it the plug wires going straight into this junction box unit that's off the underneath of the right fender well. I removed that when I removed the engine.<P>2. A Lot of the wires (including a thick pink)are going into this piece that goes to the junction box. So I am assuming I have to connect the junction box back on?<P>3. My starter motor - sold to me as a tilton but not brand name on it - looks just like a tilton BUT... the posts on the back of it (selenoid) have the SAME SIZE posts, one of which has a 1" think wire that goes to the starter itself. Then there is this little spade like connector on top of the selenoid.<BR>SO I got confused as to what wire goes where.<P>4. I am not using the a/c for the time being.<P>5. Do I need to hook up those 2 vacuum lines that go against the front of the trunk?<P>6. I will keep my day job.<P>Thank you. I tried not to bug you because I bought the kit from a friend. I believe in receiving support when I pay for stuff. So thanks for offering to help.<BR>||||reg||10
