Z||000013||Zorba||11-02-2000||12:46 PM||||Further explanation:<P>I have wired the wires as follows:<P>1. Battery cable to the starter post. The empty one as shown on the picture above.<BR>2. I have one thick wire going from the alternator post to the starter, same post as the battery cable.<BR>3. There is one thin wire attached to the red alternator wire that goes into the junction box. That wire appears to be dark brown in color.<BR>4. I have the big THICK purple wire connected to the spade connector on the starter. The purple wire originates from the junction box NOT the wiring harness.<BR>5. The PINK wire is also originating from the juction box and goes into the BAT (+) post of the back of the HEI distributor<BR>6. I have a set of dangling fusible links by the junction box. These aren't connected anywhere. Without running a hot wire to them, I get no power inside the cabin for lights, radio, gauges, etc.<BR>7. Turning the ignition key does nothing.<BR>8. The battery is showing 12V of charge<P>There is a thin "RED" wire coming from the <BR>wiring harness, the ECM, which is "hot" with the ignition "ON".<P>IF I splice both PURPLE and PINK WIRES and provide power to them with the ignition in the "ON" Position...could this solve my problem?<P>Thank You.||||reg||1
